People don't need help
hitting the snooze button,

00:10:22.746 --> 00:10:24.836
people need help making sacrifices.

00:10:24.836 --> 00:10:27.283
So as your boy ET tells you, look,

00:10:27.283 --> 00:10:29.086
I'm not saying it's going to be easy.

00:10:29.086 --> 00:10:30.792
I didn't make up the rules.

00:10:30.792 --> 00:10:33.091
I'm not saying you don't need
a third or fourth chance,

00:10:33.091 --> 00:10:35.938
I didn't make up the rules,
but what I'm telling you is,

00:10:35.938 --> 00:10:38.829
life is like track and field, and Rio.

00:10:38.829 --> 00:10:41.326
You don't always get another one.

00:10:41.326 --> 00:10:43.013
You don't always get a second one.

00:10:43.013 --> 00:10:44.533
You don't always get a third one.

00:10:44.533 --> 00:10:46.030
You don't always get a fourth one.

00:10:46.030 --> 00:10:47.702
Yup, it's tough, it's hard.

00:10:47.702 --> 00:10:50.454
Listen to me, if it was
easy to stay focused

00:10:50.454 --> 00:10:52.734
on that start line, everybody would do it.

00:10:52.734 --> 00:10:55.893
If it was easy to jump
off with a great start,

00:10:55.893 --> 00:10:57.306
everybody would do it!

00:10:57.306 --> 00:10:58.978
I'm not telling you it's going to be easy

00:10:58.978 --> 00:11:00.310
to get up at three o'clock in the morning.

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:02.096
I'm not telling you it's
going to be easy to sacrifice.

00:11:02.096 --> 00:11:04.124
I'm not telling you it's
going to be easy to grind.

00:11:04.124 --> 00:11:06.623
I'm not telling you it's going to be easy.

00:11:06.623 --> 00:11:11.385
But I can tell you this: it
will be worth the sacrifice.

00:11:11.385 --> 00:11:14.300
If you can grind your way through it.

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:18.383
So like Usain Bolt, no
excuses, just adjustments.

00:11:19.484 --> 00:11:21.239
Execute, my friend.

00:11:21.239 --> 00:11:22.072
Execute.

00:11:22.924 --> 00:11:26.012
I did not become successful
with two family household,

00:11:26.012 --> 00:11:28.095
with the income $250,000.

00:11:29.323 --> 00:11:30.974
I was homeless.

00:11:30.974 --> 00:11:33.607
I was knocked out, I was
kicked out of school.

00:11:33.607 --> 00:11:35.191
I was told never to return,

00:11:35.191 --> 00:11:37.282
I did this in the midst of trials,

00:11:37.282 --> 00:11:38.735
in the midst of tribulation.

00:11:38.735 --> 00:11:41.545
Nobody gave me this, I earned it.

00:11:41.545 --> 00:11:44.466
Life wasn't a crystal stair for me,

00:11:44.466 --> 00:11:47.653
didn't nobody give me a
network, I earned the network.

00:11:47.653 --> 00:11:48.646
I know Warren Buffet

00:11:48.646 --> 00:11:50.518
because I worked my way to Warren Buffet.

00:11:50.518 --> 00:11:53.527
I worked my way to Dan Gilbert,
I worked my way to the NBA,

00:11:53.527 --> 00:11:55.159
I worked my way to the NFL.

00:11:55.159 --> 00:11:57.325
Everybody say,"E, how
did you crack the code?"

00:11:57.325 --> 00:11:59.215
I grinded my way through the code!

00:11:59.215 --> 00:12:00.897
That's how I cracked it.

00:12:00.897 --> 00:12:03.857
I got up everyday at three,
every Monday I grind,

00:12:03.857 --> 00:12:04.694
Tuesday I grind, Wedn-

00:12:04.694 --> 00:12:06.808
I don't care what the economy is doing,

00:12:06.808 --> 00:12:08.359
I don't care who the President is,

00:12:08.359 --> 00:12:09.857
I don't care who the governor is,

00:12:09.857 --> 00:12:12.677
I don't care who the mayor is.

00:12:12.677 --> 00:12:15.320
My mamma ain't counting on the governor,

00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:17.146
my wife ain't counting on the President

00:12:17.146 --> 00:12:18.663
of the United States of America.

00:12:18.663 --> 00:12:20.422
My wife ain't counting on the mayor,

00:12:20.422 --> 00:12:22.143
my wife ain't counting
on the commissioner.

00:12:22.143 --> 00:12:23.696
My wife counting on me.

00:12:23.696 --> 00:12:25.855
When I walk out that
house, she's counting on me

00:12:25.855 --> 00:12:27.560
to bring home the bacon.

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:29.112
Listen to me, guys:

00:12:29.112 --> 00:12:31.742
environment is everything.

00:12:31.742 --> 00:12:34.022
Alright, "ET, why is
environment everything?"

00:12:34.022 --> 00:12:36.566
Guys, two things, real quick, why.

00:12:36.566 --> 00:12:40.774
Because expectation and
exposure, are you hearing me?

00:12:40.774 --> 00:12:43.559
Expectation and exposure.

00:12:43.559 --> 00:12:45.484
So, catch what I'm saying, right?

00:12:45.484 --> 00:12:47.528
This is why you got to get
out of your environment

00:12:47.528 --> 00:12:50.394
and get into a new environment
if you going to blow up.

00:12:50.394 --> 00:12:53.417
So you got KG, who'd never
been to Boston before.

00:12:53.417 --> 00:12:55.862
Oh, come on, come on!

00:12:55.862 --> 00:12:59.184
You got Jesus Shuttlesworth,
never been to Boston before.

00:12:59.184 --> 00:13:02.564
You got Paul Peirce, who's
been in Boston the whole time.

00:13:02.564 --> 00:13:04.740
So they ask the question:

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:07.390
Paul Peirce, what's the
difference between Boston

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:08.538
and everywhere else?

00:13:08.538 --> 00:13:10.507
He said, "Expectations."

00:13:10.507 --> 00:13:14.608
Here in Boston, you are
expected, listen to me,

00:13:14.608 --> 00:13:17.865
don't nobody get excited
about having a winning season,

00:13:17.865 --> 00:13:20.066
don't nobody get excited
about the playoffs,

00:13:20.066 --> 00:13:21.293
don't nobody get excited

00:13:21.293 --> 00:13:23.034
about the Eastern Conference Finals.

00:13:23.034 --> 00:13:26.745
In Boston, the expectation
is to win it all.

00:13:26.745 --> 00:13:29.193
Are you hearing me?
It's a different level.

00:13:29.193 --> 00:13:32.283
There's levels to this, so
much so that Paul Peirce

00:13:32.283 --> 00:13:36.412
says we don't even hang up
Eastern Conference banners.

00:13:36.412 --> 00:13:38.377
Like, when we win the Eastern Con--

00:13:38.377 --> 00:13:39.891
we don't even hang that up!

00:13:39.891 --> 00:13:44.362
In Boston we only hang up
Finals banners. That's it!

00:13:44.362 --> 00:13:47.232
You win the finals or
you don't win at all!

00:13:47.232 --> 00:13:48.933
Look, you think you doing it.

00:13:48.933 --> 00:13:50.622
Are you hearing me?
You think you doing it,

00:13:50.622 --> 00:13:52.770
you the first one in your
family to go to college, right?

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:55.211
So for you, you been
like, "I'm the first one."

00:13:55.211 --> 00:13:57.258
I'm the only one to ever go to college,

00:13:57.258 --> 00:13:59.130
and you think you've
done something, right?

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:00.782
You got kids when you go to college,

00:14:00.782 --> 00:14:02.978
nobody's excited about the
fact they're in college.

00:14:02.978 --> 00:14:05.826
Nobody's excited about the
fact that they graduated.

00:14:05.826 --> 00:14:07.907
They want to know, are
you going to be a doctor,

00:14:07.907 --> 00:14:09.828
you going to be a lawyer,
you going to be an engineer?

00:14:09.828 --> 00:14:11.817
It's a different level.

00:14:11.817 --> 00:14:13.591
Paul Peirce said it's environment.

00:14:13.591 --> 00:14:15.261
We not even talking about-- come on,

00:14:15.261 --> 00:14:18.215
we not even taking about
the Boston Celtics.

00:14:18.215 --> 00:14:19.967
We talking about Boston.

00:14:19.967 --> 00:14:22.636
Right up the road you got
the New England Patriots,

00:14:22.636 --> 00:14:25.165
right up the road you
got the Boston Bruins,

00:14:25.165 --> 00:14:27.446
right up the road you got Harvard.

00:14:27.446 --> 00:14:31.156
This environment has
a level of expectation

00:14:31.156 --> 00:14:32.677
that's out of this world.

00:14:32.677 --> 00:14:35.849
And your problem is you're
in an environment of average,

00:14:35.849 --> 00:14:37.221
and you good.

00:14:37.221 --> 00:14:39.358
And so you good with being good

00:14:39.358 --> 00:14:41.604
because your environment is average.

00:14:41.604 --> 00:14:44.007
Are you hearing me? So
you think good is great.

00:14:44.007 --> 00:14:46.471
Now you told yourself that good is great.

00:14:46.471 --> 00:14:49.083
Look, I grew up in Detroit,
no disrespect, right?

00:14:49.083 --> 00:14:51.917
But the Lions, they just trying
to have a winning season.

00:14:51.917 --> 00:14:53.989
They just trying to
make it to the playoffs.

00:14:53.989 --> 00:14:55.153
Are you hearing me?

00:14:55.153 --> 00:14:57.177
They just trying to
make it to the playoffs.

00:14:57.177 --> 00:14:59.456
If you are a Cowboy, it's win it all.

00:14:59.456 --> 00:15:01.566
If you are a Laker, it's win it all.

00:15:01.566 --> 00:15:05.414
If you in Boston, it's win
it all, guys! Listen to me!

00:15:05.414 --> 00:15:09.348
It's not just about expectation,
it's about exposure.

00:15:09.348 --> 00:15:12.316
And when you are a Boston
Celtic you been exposed.

00:15:12.316 --> 00:15:14.779
When you were a Laker you been exposed

00:15:14.779 --> 00:15:16.889
to the greatest of the great, right?

00:15:16.889 --> 00:15:18.911
And so there's a level of expectation.

00:15:18.911 --> 00:15:21.530
I'll never forget when
Kobe came to the NBA,

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:24.300
Kobe said, "I'm not playing
for the Charlotte Hornets,

00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:26.338
"I'm not playing for
the Charlotte Hornets,

00:15:26.338 --> 00:15:28.044
"I want to be a Laker."

00:15:28.044 --> 00:15:30.135
And when you walk through
that Laker stadium,

00:15:30.135 --> 00:15:32.110
when you walk through that Boston stadium,

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:33.879
all you see is great.

00:15:33.879 --> 00:15:36.447
And so because you're
being exposed to great,

00:15:36.447 --> 00:15:38.135
all you know is great.

00:15:38.135 --> 00:15:42.018
When I came to Michigan State
I was exposed to greatness,

00:15:42.018 --> 00:15:44.670
I was exposed to Tom Izzo,

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:46.972
I was exposed to Mark Dantonio,

00:15:46.972 --> 00:15:49.114
I was exposed to the Rose Bowl,

00:15:49.114 --> 00:15:51.513
I was exposed to the Final Four.

00:15:51.513 --> 00:15:54.633
Are you hearing what I'm
saying? I got around greatness

00:15:54.633 --> 00:15:57.171
and so I had no choice but to be great.

00:15:57.171 --> 00:15:58.791
So I ask you the question:

00:15:58.791 --> 00:16:02.421
what's your expectations?
What do you want for yourself?

00:16:02.421 --> 00:16:04.159
What do you want for your family?

00:16:04.159 --> 00:16:06.052
What do you want for the next generation?

00:16:06.052 --> 00:16:08.125
What do you expect of yourself?

00:16:08.125 --> 00:16:09.492
Listen to me very closely,

00:16:09.492 --> 00:16:11.486
it's not what coach wants for you,

00:16:11.486 --> 00:16:13.541
it's not what your mamma want for you,

00:16:13.541 --> 00:16:15.314
it's not what your daddy want for you,

00:16:15.314 --> 00:16:17.050
it's not what your teacher wants for you.

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:18.887
It's not what everybody
else wants for you.

00:16:18.887 --> 00:16:21.949
What do you want for
yourself? What drives you?

00:16:21.949 --> 00:16:25.860
What pushes you, what motivates
you, what makes you tick?

00:16:25.860 --> 00:16:30.181
What activates you? What are
you expectations for yourself?

00:16:30.181 --> 00:16:33.368
And then ask yourself, when
you wake up every morning,

00:16:33.368 --> 00:16:35.092
what are you being exposed to?

00:16:35.092 --> 00:16:37.338
And if you don't like the places you see,

00:16:37.338 --> 00:16:38.975
if you don't like where you going,

00:16:38.975 --> 00:16:41.116
if you don't like what
life is showing you,

00:16:41.116 --> 00:16:44.120
get in an environment of greatness

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:46.826
so you can be exposed to greatness.

00:16:46.826 --> 00:16:50.208
And by beholding, we become changed.

00:16:50.208 --> 00:16:52.875
By beholding, we become changed.

00:16:53.752 --> 00:16:55.669
What are you beholding?

00:16:57.633 --> 00:17:00.310
Where your focus goes, your energy flows.

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:02.417
And so if you focusing in on the negative,

00:17:02.417 --> 00:17:03.668
guess what's going to happen?

00:17:03.668 --> 00:17:05.273
Your energy is going
to go to the negative,

00:17:05.273 --> 00:17:07.868
and everything is going to be negative

00:17:07.868 --> 00:17:09.573
because that's where your focus is.

00:17:09.573 --> 00:17:11.612
That's where you energy
is flowing, listen to me.

00:17:11.612 --> 00:17:15.434
If you think about that thing,
you concentrate on winning.

00:17:15.434 --> 00:17:18.044
You concentrate on dominating.

00:17:18.044 --> 00:17:20.171
Listen to me, whatever you focus on,

00:17:20.171 --> 00:17:23.058
where your focus goes your energy flows.

00:17:23.058 --> 00:17:26.667
So we going to think about
what we thinking about.

00:17:26.667 --> 00:17:29.349
We going to think about
what we thinking about.

00:17:29.349 --> 00:17:32.054
And when we think about
those things which are pure,

00:17:32.054 --> 00:17:33.538
listen to me, come on!

00:17:33.538 --> 00:17:35.358
That stuff that's true, right?

00:17:35.358 --> 00:17:39.137
Whatsoever things are pure,
whatsoever things are true,

00:17:39.137 --> 00:17:40.860
whatsoever things are lovely,

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:43.053
whatsoever things are of good report,

00:17:43.053 --> 00:17:43.984
are you hearing me?

00:17:43.984 --> 00:17:46.615
Meditate on this stuff,
focus on this stuff,

00:17:46.615 --> 00:17:48.758
it don't mean negative
things won't happen,

00:17:48.758 --> 00:17:51.118
but we not focusing on
it. Are you hearing me?

00:17:51.118 --> 00:17:54.053
It don't mean that negative
things won't transpire,

00:17:54.053 --> 00:17:57.109
that as you go through the day
something bad won't happen,

00:17:57.109 --> 00:17:59.120
but we not going to meditate on it.

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:01.044
We going to focus on what's positive,

00:18:01.044 --> 00:18:02.917
we going to focus on what's good, right?

00:18:02.917 --> 00:18:04.386
And when we focus on that,

00:18:04.386 --> 00:18:05.886
that's where our energy's going to go.

00:18:05.886 --> 00:18:07.591
And what's going to happen is the outcomes

00:18:07.591 --> 00:18:09.143
are going to reflect our thinking.

00:18:09.143 --> 00:18:11.946
I'm feel your pain, you
like, "E, it ain't easy!

00:18:11.946 --> 00:18:14.375
"You don't know where I come from, ET!

00:18:14.375 --> 00:18:16.906
"It ain't just that easy
to go from where I am

00:18:16.906 --> 00:18:19.269
"to get this new circle of influence."

00:18:19.269 --> 00:18:21.312
I feel you, yup, yup, yup.

00:18:21.312 --> 00:18:25.327
I've read the comments, like,
"ET, you don't understand, E,

00:18:25.327 --> 00:18:28.361
"you don't know the
environment that I was born in.

00:18:28.361 --> 00:18:31.974
"ET you don't know how hard it
is to get to where you said."

00:18:31.974 --> 00:18:33.358
Look, I get it!

00:18:33.358 --> 00:18:35.724
And then I got teachers
that have called me,

00:18:35.724 --> 00:18:38.711
teachers that have reached
out like, "ET, you don't know

00:18:38.711 --> 00:18:40.583
"where these kids come from, ET!

00:18:40.583 --> 00:18:42.875
"You don't understand
their circumstances, ET!

00:18:42.875 --> 00:18:45.712
"You giving them this
dream that they can get

00:18:45.712 --> 00:18:47.185
"in a different circle."

00:18:47.185 --> 00:18:48.544
Listen to me, listen to me very--

00:18:48.544 --> 00:18:50.302
whatcha want me to do? Come one!

00:18:50.302 --> 00:18:52.295
Whatcha want me to do,
whatcha want me to tell you

00:18:52.295 --> 00:18:54.151
to accept the life that you've been given?

00:18:54.151 --> 00:18:55.379
Huh? Whatcha want?

00:18:55.379 --> 00:18:57.273
You want me to tell you to give up? Huh?

00:18:57.273 --> 00:18:58.693
You want me to tell you to quit?

00:18:58.693 --> 00:19:00.665
Is that what you want me to say?

00:19:00.665 --> 00:19:03.799
You want to hear ET say,
"It's alright to give up.

00:19:03.799 --> 00:19:05.407
"It's alright to surrender."

00:19:05.407 --> 00:19:07.143
That's what you want me to say?

00:19:07.143 --> 00:19:09.222
Well listen to me, bra,
I can't tell you that.

00:19:09.222 --> 00:19:12.411
But what I can tell you
is this: that I did it.

00:19:12.411 --> 00:19:14.587
And I used one thing,
I know it ain't easy.

00:19:14.587 --> 00:19:18.163
I come from where you come
from. I been there, I done that.

00:19:18.163 --> 00:19:20.709
It wasn't easy for me to
get to where I am right now.

00:19:20.709 --> 00:19:23.243
I used two things and two things only.

00:19:23.243 --> 00:19:25.827
Ain't nobody give me no
money to get out the hood.

00:19:25.827 --> 00:19:27.125
Didn't nobody give me to resources

00:19:27.125 --> 00:19:28.761
to get out of that abandoned building.

00:19:28.761 --> 00:19:30.870
I used two things and two things only:

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:34.465
one, my mind. I envisioned
myself getting out.

00:19:34.465 --> 00:19:35.849
And two, my heart.

00:19:35.849 --> 00:19:37.602
And you can't measure that.

00:19:37.602 --> 00:19:39.526
That's right, and you can't measure that.

00:19:39.526 --> 00:19:41.652
So listen to me, I'm not
about to tell you to quit.

00:19:41.652 --> 00:19:43.392
I'm not about to tell you

00:19:43.392 --> 00:19:45.184
that you going to keep that cycle going.

00:19:45.184 --> 00:19:46.889
I'm going to tell you to break that cycle.

00:19:46.889 --> 00:19:48.016
So listen to me,

00:19:48.016 --> 00:19:49.871
you can get in a different
circle of influence.

00:19:49.871 --> 00:19:51.932
You can, you can get to another level.

00:19:51.932 --> 00:19:54.161
But it's going to take two
things. Are you hearing me?

00:19:54.161 --> 00:19:56.609
I got here from my mind,
and I envisioned it.

00:19:56.609 --> 00:19:59.290
I saw myself when I was still homeless,

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:01.278
when I was still a high school dropout,

00:20:01.278 --> 00:20:03.386
when I was sleeping in
abandoned buildings,

00:20:03.386 --> 00:20:04.839
and eating out of trash cans.

00:20:04.839 --> 00:20:07.573
I saw myself someday being
where I am right now.

00:20:07.573 --> 00:20:10.107
I don't care where you
are, use what you got

00:20:10.107 --> 00:20:11.524
to get what you want.

00:20:11.524 --> 00:20:15.443
Use your mind, use your
vision, use your dream.

00:20:15.443 --> 00:20:17.090
I dreamed my way out the hood.

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:19.790
I dreamed my way out, and then I saw it.

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:23.098
And I would get up every
day and I would grind hard.

00:20:23.098 --> 00:20:25.075
I would grind my way through it.

00:20:25.075 --> 00:20:26.762
So listen to me, I'm
going to tell you a story.

00:20:26.762 --> 00:20:29.577
First gig I ever did
in my life was Bermuda.

00:20:29.577 --> 00:20:32.198
Listen to me, I dreamed about
Bermuda for eight months

00:20:32.198 --> 00:20:33.208
before I got there.

00:20:33.208 --> 00:20:35.620
I'm not playing with you,
I can't make this stuff up.

00:20:35.620 --> 00:20:37.376
Are you hearing me? I went to the library,

00:20:37.376 --> 00:20:38.711
and I read about it.

00:20:38.711 --> 00:20:41.294
I asked my friends that were
from Bermuda about Bermuda,

00:20:41.294 --> 00:20:43.047
and they told me about the water,

00:20:43.047 --> 00:20:44.867
and they told me about the palm trees,

00:20:44.867 --> 00:20:46.894
